<title>USA: First Merchants completes securitization.</title>
<headline>First Merchants completes securitization.</headline>
<dateline>DEERFIELD, Ill. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Merchants Acceptance Corp said it completed on March 31 a $97.6 million asset securitization through the sale of automobile receivables-backed notes and certificates.</p>
<p>Of the securities, $68 million Class A-1 notes have a floating rate (LIBOR, plus 13 basis points), and $29.6 million Class A-2 notes have a fixed rate of 6.75 percent. First Merchants will act as servicer for this portfolio.</p>
<p>Proceeds of the offering will be used to pay down First Merchants' senior bank line.</p>
<p>The notes and certificates were issued by First Merchants Auto Trust 1997-1 A, a trust formed specifically for the purpose of the securitization structure.</p>
